can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}))=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}))=\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}))=-\\frac{2z}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}-(1)^{2}}=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1) & =\\frac{2(-1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}-(1)^{2}}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) & =-\\frac{2(1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}-(1)^{2}}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1)+(y+1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) \\\\ w & =2(x-1)-2(y+1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w & =2x-2-2y-2-2z+2 \\\\ -2x+2y+2z+w+2 & =0 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z-w-2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407546 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407548 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407546 1062 #uuid "0eadd7d5-26a1-573f-b533-83cfbfb498b9" 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407546 1063 #edb/ref 17592186342103 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407547 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407550 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407547 1062 #uuid "2b51d9b4-6f4d-519a-946f-18af30633fc4" 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407547 1063 #edb/ref 17592186323970 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407548 1062 #uuid "32cd70ef-6665-5a4e-a0ab-b70e5098e66f" 13194139533544 17592186045585 true] [17592186407548 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265754 13194139533544 17592186045585 tr